# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Content pipeline sources. Set EITHER the *_REPO_PATH pair (local checkouts)
# OR GITHUB_TOKEN (the pipeline shallow-clones both repos itself).
# None of these are needed for `npm run dev` or `npm run build` — the site
# renders from the committed snapshot in src/generated/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local checkout of duettoresearch/APEX.
APEX_REPO_PATH=/absolute/path/to/APEX

# Git ref to read the APEX checkout at. Defaults to origin/main.
# APEX_REF=origin/main

# Local checkout of duettoresearch/apex-companion.
APEX_COMPANION_REPO_PATH=/absolute/path/to/apex-companion

# Fallback source: a token with `repo` scope on both private repositories.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx

# Required only to install @duettoresearch/marketing-ds from GitHub Packages.
# The design system is currently vendored (src/vendor/marketing-ds/), so this
# is unused until the package is actually published.
# NODE_AUTH_TOKEN=ghp_xxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leak-gate private denylist.
#
# The leak gate has two tiers. Generic SHAPE patterns live in
# scripts/lib/forbidden.ts and are committed, because they disclose nothing.
# The specific instances — people, internal project codenames, exact chat
# channel ids, personal handles — must NOT be committed: this repository is
# public, so a committed denylist publishes what it exists to suppress.
#
# Supply them here (newline- or comma-separated) or in a gitignored
# .leak-denylist.local file at the repo root. Both are merged.
#
# `npm run content` and `npm run sync` FAIL when neither is present, because
# generating a snapshot without the full gate is how a name reaches the site.
# `npm test` and `npm run build` run fine without it — they validate a snapshot
# that was generated on a machine that had it.
LEAK_DENYLIST=

# Override the default denylist file path (.leak-denylist.local).
# LEAK_DENYLIST_FILE=.leak-denylist.local

# Generate anyway with generic patterns only. Understand what stops being
# checked before setting this.
# LEAK_DENYLIST_OPTIONAL=1
